AI Model TF September, 2026 B.6.1 Judge Scoring Prompt The judge prompt ( EVAL SYSTEM PROMPT in trainer.py) instructs the judge model to grade a response on a 0–10 scale while remaining blind to the gold answer. Its key requirements are: (i) solve the problem independently before grading, never assuming the model’s answer is correct; (ii) 10 means the final answer is correct, 0 means wrong or missing, with partial credit (1–9) for substantive progress on incorrect solutions; (iii) the feedback must locate the methodological error and how to fix it without ever revealing or hinting at the final answer (no numbers, letters, or expressions); (iv) no restating of the question or response. Question: {question}

Response: {response}

Evaluate this response. Provide detailed feedback and a score. The judge returns its output in the format <FEEDBACK>...</FEEDBACK><SCORE>0-10</SCORE>; the score drives judge-select (Appendix B.3) and the feedback becomes the input to the backward pass below. B.6.2 Backward (Text Gradient) Prompt The backward prompt (BACKWARD SYSTEM PROMPT in llm backward prompts.py) asks the en- gine to act as the “gradient” with respect to the context variable: given the current system prompt, the question, the model’s response, and the judge feedback, produce criticism of the context—strategies, explanations, and methods to change—but never a rewritten version of the variable (that is the optimizer’s job). It carries the same
